The game flourished in the 18th century, yet there are not as many variations of this game as with other casino games that have been around for some time. There are small differences between the roulette variants, but these differences have a huge impact on the advantage for the casino.
You could say that today there are 3 main variations of roulette: European, American and French. You can see the difference by the number of zeros on the wheel.
In multi-ball roulette you have the option to spin the wheel with a maximum of 3 balls, giving you 3 winning results. If you want to play with more than 1 ball, your bet is divided into two or three equal parts, depending on the number of balls used.
No zero roulette games, as the name implies, have no zero on the wheel, only 36 numbers to bet on. This is a special innovation in the casino industry, as no zero roulette rules out the house edge.
This is a roulette variant that has been developed to simplify the betting process and to be able to play on the smaller screens of mobile devices. The game has exactly the same rules as regular roulette, but the difference is in the number of spaces on the wheel.
