Company News Fresh, Nutrition, Safty, this kind of canned food must be what you want!
The main reason most people abandon canned food is because they think canned food is not fresh.
The reason for the long shelf life of canned food is that canned food undergoes vacuum sealing and high-temperature sterilization in the production process. The vacuum environment prevents the high-temperature sterilized food from contacting the bacteria in the air, preventing the food from being contaminated by bacteria at the source.
In 1810, when canned food was born, modern food preservatives such as sorbic acid and benzoic acid had not been invented at all. In order to extend the shelf life of food, people used canning technology to make food into cans.
The main reason why many people don’t like canned food is that they think canned food is not fresh. Most people subconsciously equate “long shelf life” with “not fresh”, which is actually wrong.
How can they be fresher than most fruits and vegetables in a short time! After all, before consumers bought it, the so-called fresh fruits and vegetables had already experienced the 9981 difficulty and lost a lot of nutrients.edit In fact, most canned food is more nutritious than the fresh food you eat
We have already mentioned one of the reasons for the long shelf life of cans, that is, vacuum environment, and the second is high temperature sterilization. High temperature sterilization, also known as pasteurization, allows high temperature sterilized food to no longer contact with bacteria in the air, which is called preventing food from being contaminated by bacteria from the source.
Canned food is certainly not as nutritious as fresh food!
In fact, the processing temperature of canned meat is about 120 ℃, the processing temperature of canned vegetables and fruits is not more than 100 ℃, while the temperature of our daily cooking is more than 300 ℃. Therefore, the loss of vitamins in the process of canning will exceed the loss in frying, frying, frying and boiling?
