A closed-or managed open-loop shipping system: Once reusable transport packaging is shipped to its final destination and contents are removed, the empty transport packaging components are collected, staged, and returned without a great deal of time and cost. Reverse logistics—or the return trip for empty packaging components—must be repeated in a closed-or managed open-loop shipping system.
Inbound freight can be picked up and consolidated for delivery on a more frequent just-in-time basis.
