Indeed, when we speak with anger, we come to say things that we may regret later. Similarly, when we are in pain or when we feel fear, we tend to react excessively and unreasonably.
At the same time, you have to choose whether or not you want to share what you feel. Warning !
In other words, it is important to determine the why of such and such an act. In addition, it is sometimes necessary to remain discreet on the objective that one wishes to reach by sharing an emotion in particular.
That is why it is necessary to choose one's language and reflect on what one is going to say. The first rule to respect is to express the problem in an objective way.
Nonverbal language is often easier to understand than words. For example, it is impossible to know if a person speaks with humor or seriousness if he does not indicate it through his attitudes or his intonation.
Thus, when your interlocutor has become aware of your feelings, you must express the desired action. In addition, additional details and conditions concerning its realization must be added.
All this requires personal development work. One must learn to know his reactions to such and such a situation and his emotional gestures.
Finally, we must not be content to criticize. It is also necessary to present a solution.
