When you want to settle in France, there are several ways to obtain a valid driver's license. Foreign nationals will then have to find the best option for their own situation, and for their projects.
Whether you are a European citizen or not, you can exchange your driving license for a French title. This can be done under certain conditions.
Foreign nationals who have recently settled in France and who have a non-European driving license are obliged to exchange it for a French license. This allows them to move and to drive legally on French soil.
The formalities to be completed to exchange his driving license
This measure is not mandatory, but it can become so when the person concerned is restricted, canceled, suspended or lost points.
Proof of payment of the regional tax (non-existent depending on the locality);
The escort must therefore be the owner of the driving license for at least five years. He must not ask the plaintiff for any compensation.
It is quite possible to continue driving when you arrive in France for a longer or shorter stay. It is important to take the necessary steps to get your driver's license, or exchange the one you have against a French title.
