In this article, we explain how to write an email to justify a delay, whether it is a delay in the morning or a delay in the deadlines for rendering your work.
This may be because you are late for work because of an unexpected event, or because you have been late for work. In any case, it is important to justify your delay for valid reasons and to apologize to your supervisor.
However, it is still important to justify it to testify to your good faith.
When you justify a delay by e-mailyou must support your justification so that it is credible, because you do not have the possibility to convince by the expressions of the face. First of all, it is important to begin by apologizing for your delay.
If you are late due to medical appointments (such as a blood test), you should be able to show a medical certificate. Similarly, if you have made a late work because you did not have the response from your contact earlier: attach a copy of the late response to your email.
Here is a model to follow to justify a delay by email, if we take the example of a medical appointment that lasted longer than expected.
I made an appointment for a routine medical examination at 8h, which took longer than expected. Attached is the certificate of this examination.
