Discover the right solution! To express oneself or to lock oneself up?
On the one hand, to express it is to liberate oneself, it brings incredible well-being. But on the other hand, it is often said that being quiet is the best option when one is overwhelmed by unpleasant emotions.
Should we then repress his feelings and shut up?
This can only result in additional stress. On the other hand, we must act intelligently by trying to reveal what we feel in a constructive way.
Without question, before saying anything, the first thing to do is to identify what you really feel in your heart. This is called taking a step back.
It is by taking a step back that we can better understand the situation and identify his emotions. We must also try to control them if necessary.
It is out of the question to make a decision lightly. If one decides to reveal one's emotions, one must question the reasons and the consequences.
To be clearer, we must remember the facts as they are. For example, you have an appointment with your college at 8h.
It is better to say: "We had an appointment at 8h; it's 8h 30, I've been waiting for you for half an hour. " This is called expressing itself clearly and objectively.
But that does not mean that we have to hide what we feel. Whether it's disappointment or anger, it's important to let your caller know.
That said, before starting, one must first recognize his signs of bodily emotions and triggers. This is how we manage and manage them better.
Obviously, to express oneself in a constructive way, one must be prepared to face one's interlocutor, hence the need to take a step back. We must give ourselves the time to learn how to express emotions with sobriety.
In short, expressing one's emotions in constructive ways is a difficult task that requires real work on oneself. One must take a step back, learn to control emotions and emotional gestures.
