Many health facilities are public, and care is very good. The World Health Organization recognizes the French health system as the most efficient in terms of organization of health care and dispensing.
The first level groups the compulsory basic health insurance schemes. Three are principal and others, more specific, come attached to it.
The third level of the French health system is intended for those who wish to further strengthen their coverage. Most often, they target specific positions such as soft medicine or dentures.
There are two kinds of doctors: those who respect the rates of health insurance and those who fix their fees themselves.
Joining the social security system allows for partial reimbursement of the costs of care. The co-payment is the sum remaining due which is borne by the patient, or the complementary (or mutual) thereof.
Secondly, the secondment of an employee in France can not exceed a period of two years. In such cases, it is essential to have a long-stay visa.
Students older than 28 are therefore obliged to join the primary health insurance fund.
European pensioners wishing to settle in France can transfer their rights to health insurance. For non-European residents, it is not possible to transfer these rights.
The French health system, and public health in general, are elements put forward in France. It is important to learn about the necessary steps to take when you want to to settle in France for a more or less prolonged period.
