Constructive criticism is an art. It must enable the person concerned to identify his or her weaknesses and the gaps that must be filled in on different points.
Could she get angry?
Otherwise, we run the risk of launching hurtful and demotivating words. In order to avoid this regrettable mistake that can ruin the relationship, you have to wait for the storm to calm down before saying anything.
· Always rely on facts
When one makes a constructive criticism, one must accept that the person concerned also has his say. In other words, you have to be open to discussion and let it speak freely.
· Highlight your strengths
By the way, remembering things well that the person has done is a better way to manage your anger. You will forget your disappointments, because you believe that it will be able to change things and solve the problem.
This means that you must remain available if he needs help or if he encounters a problem again. Obviously, it is impossible to reach out to him if he has not changed his behavior.
If negative emotions come to overwhelm you, avoid answering immediately. The best is to take a step back and analyze the content of the criticism received.
