Email has long been an essential tool for business communications, but a survey conducted by Sendmail. Revealed that it caused tension, confusion or other negative consequences to 64% of professionals.
And how can you write emails that give the desired results?
One of the biggest sources of stress at work is the sheer volume of emails people receive. So, before you start writing an email, ask yourself, "Is it really necessary?"
Whenever possible, give the bad news in person. It helps you communicate with empathy, compassion and understanding and redeem yourself if your message has been wrongly taken.
A newspaper title has two functions: it captures your attention and summarizes the article so you can decide whether to read it or not. The subject of your e-mail message should do the same thing.
You may want to include the date in the subject if your message is part of a series of regular emails, such as a weekly project report. For a message that requires a response, you can also include a call to action, such as "Please before November 7."
Unlike traditional letters, sending multiple emails does not cost more than sending one. So, if you need to communicate with someone on a number of different topics, consider writing a separate email for each.
Thank you for sending this report last week. I read it yesterday and I feel that chapter 2 requires more specific information about our sales figures.
Please, let me know if you are available.
I also think that the tone could be more formal.
Thank you for your hard work!
Also note that in the good example above, Camille specified what she wanted Michelin to do (in this case, modify the report). If you help people know what you want, there is a better chance that they will give it to you.
People often think that emails can be less formal than traditional letters. But the messages you send are a reflection of your own professionalism, values and attention to detail are important, so a certain level of formality is needed.
Close your message with "Sincerely," "Good day / evening to you" or "Good to you," depending on the situation.
Your choice of words, length of sentence, punctuation and capitalization can easily be misinterpreted without visual and auditory cues. In the first example below, Louise might think Yann is frustrated or angry, but in reality, he feels good.
Thank you for your hard work on this report. Could you provide me your version before 17 hours, so that I do not miss my deadline?
Most of us spend a good part of their day reading and composing emails. But the messages we send can be confusing to others.
Make your emails concise and precise. Send them only to people who really need to see them and clearly indicate what you would like the recipient to do next.
The French language is certainly not the easiest to learn when it is foreign to us. For this reason, it may be wise to rely on qualitative French resources and some supports of different natures to learn French simply and effectively.
Learning French, if it is not your mother tongue, requires a slightly different approach to the methods used in France. It is important to know the many rules of grammar, especially because of the complexity and specificities of the language of Molière.
French is a language spoken in Europe, but also in various parts of the world. France is a world power that opens up to a wide cultural diversity and its language offers different business opportunities in Europe, but also in the rest of the world.
How to go about working the French language?
To learn French, it is possible to rely on resources to acquire the knowledge necessary to master this language. The Internet is a great tool when used for learning and learning in multiple domains.
Through this selection of websites, it is possible to discover all aspects of the French language as its grammar, vocabulary, expressions or the principles of conjugation. These sites target their content and resources in French to adult students.
The Bonjour de France website provides Internet users with a set of educational sheets ready to be used and exploited. They can then be offered to students or simply worked independently to better assimilate different aspects of the French language through distinct categories of progression: beginner, intermediate, autonomous, advanced and expert.
It was developed by the French Embassy in Republic of Ireland, in collaboration with the University of Maynooth as well as the Irish Ministry of Education. Although it is primarily intended for French-speaking assistants, it can also provide important information and pedagogical resources for English-speaking students who are looking to learn French with relevant and effective documents.
It is a platform for learning different languages. It incorporates a wealth of linguistic content such as texts and audio, as well as tools for learning vocabulary such as exercises, dictionaries, monitoring of achievements ... Tutors even offer discussion sessions as well as custom fixes to platform users.
EduFLE.net is a collaborative website developed for teachers and students of FLE (French as a Foreign Language). It is possible to find internship reports, articles of contributors as well as didactic files.
In addition to lessons and exercises, it is also possible to benefit from visual and sound resources to learn French. Podcasts, video, flashcards ... sites offering alternative resources are numerous and generally very well designed.
To remain motivated and to continue its efforts, the learning of the French language must remain a pleasure and a constant amusement. Some sites offer to learn French with creativity, a little humor and a touch of lightness.
Thanks to its "French and you" section, the Cia France website offers Internet users a variety of interesting games and exercises to apply their knowledge of the French language. It offers timed QCMs, games called "parachute Roger" or "stop the train", but also other activities.
Knowing how to form sentences in French and understand the statements made by other people are two notions that are fully part of French learning. But students who wish to master this language must also work their spoken French.
Once again, the TV5Monde site is distinguished by the precision of its content, and the quality of the resources available to learn French. Different memos are available and they are all accompanied by a video specifically dedicated to the pronunciation of a sound.
French is a language rather complicated to assimilate, and for which each exercise is useful. Working on pronunciation of words is very important when you want to learn French and make yourself understood by Francophones.
Acapela is a site dedicated to the pronunciation of texts written in French. It allows students to listen to a text written by them.
Tripod is a site offering phonetics courses for beginner level students. The exercises he puts online are interactive and benefit from specific answers.
This site is intended for children who are about to go to France or a French speaking country. He brings a lot of knowledge and reads, listens and shares resources to learn French around the theme of travel.
Work as a team and remotely with Slack
In each workspace created by a company on the platform, it is possible to create specific exchange zones called "chains". Themes can be assigned to them so that they can be grouped according to activities within a company.
Those who wish to have access to a channel must first have permission. Each member of a group can also create a discussion chain.
For example, to notify a unique person in a chain, you must type @ followed by the name of the person you are looking for. To notify all members of a chain, there is the command @ nom-de-la-chaine.
Can be opened on a Smartphone, it also allows you to work from anywhere. In addition, it offers the possibility of integrating several tools such as Dropbox, Skype, GitHub ...
