Why is it interesting to come to work in France?
France is a European country where work is interesting, and there are many possibilities. Apart from the dream that it generates in the minds of many Foreign nationalsit is above all an economically strong country that tends to offer important protections to employees.
Young foreign graduates are particularly well received in the area. Their knowledge, skills and vision are strong added values and the government and employers are well aware of this.
This makes it possible to earn a living without having to accumulate several jobs, and to ensure a minimum income at the end of each month. Moreover, it is quite possible to combine several jobs for those who wish to devote themselves fully to their professional life.
The "made in France"Is a pledge of quality appreciated at its fair value around the world. Craftsmen working in France are very conscientious and always offer high quality products and services.
This is largely due to the health system and the quality of care provided. Many foreign nationals choose to come to settle in France to benefit from this quality of life.
Managers have a key role in managing teams, but their place is not always easy.
This is not without consequences on the atmosphere within the company and on the quality of the work.
Accept the fact that he is your superior:
For a team to work effectively, it must be led by a leader, as is the case during a work in group.
Do not see your manager as an all-powerful person:
Your manager is not overpowered, he too is under pressure from his superiors.
In this case, one must know how to show patience and empathy.
In front of a manager too demanding, even authoritarian, you can forget that it is a human like the others.
So you must keep in mind that if there is a conflict, they are not always accountable to you and that you too may have your responsibilities that you will have to assume.
To know how to say stop:
Do not wait for the situation to escalate to talk about it.
In both home and work environments, knowing how to listen can solve or avoid many problems and alleviate many situations. This is why everyone needs to learn to listen to others in order to better understand what they are saying, in a spirit of constructive dialogue.
That means, do not think about what you'll be able to answer, but first try to understand his situation. Giving him a listening ear is indeed the only way to help him, which makes you forget your own concerns to better focus on his own.
Being able to listen also means looking serenely and quietly at the other person while she speaks without trying to dominate or judge her. Indeed, if your attitude shows the opposite, it can mean to your interlocutor that it annoys you and it will cut short the maintenance or the conversation.
So, he will know that you really listen to him and that he will not have to always repeat the same thing in case of complaints.
Without agreeing with your interlocutor, you can listen to it, but instead of objecting, you can see the situation from your point of view. By proceeding as such, you are sure to understand it better and to take another view of your point of view.
Some cases, however, are exceptions to the rule. Indeed, although it is a know-how or a disposition to put oneself in relation with the other, having this listening ability should not be confused with invasion or indifference.
