E-mail is fabulous because you do not have to be available at the same time as your contact to communicate. This allows us to move the issues forward when our colleagues are not available or on the other side of the world.
In addition, emails are too easily misunderstood. A recent Sendmail study found that 64% of people sent or received an email that caused anger or unintentional confusion.
Initially, you may need as much time to write short emails as to write long emails. However, even if this is the case, you will help your colleagues, customers or employees to be more productive, because you will add less space to their inbox, which will help them respond more quickly.
What do I expect from the recipient?
Use the "One thing at a time" rule
It's also a good time to ask yourself, "Is this email really necessary?"
When writing emails, think about your words from the reader's point of view. With everything you write, ask yourself:
Does it include ambiguous terms to specify?
Here is an empathic way to look at the world to help you get started. Most people :
Enjoy a compliment. If you can say something positive about them or their work, do it.
One way to shorten the presentations is to write them as if you are meeting face to face. You would not want to go into a five-minute monologue when you meet someone in person.
You present again to someone who already knows you are rude. If she does not know if she knows you, you can just let her check your signature.
In every email you write, you must use enough sentences to say what you need, no more. A useful practice is to limit yourself to five sentences.
There will be times when it will be impossible to keep an email containing five sentences. But in most cases, five sentences are enough.
This advice is even more relevant today, especially when writing emails.
The same is true of short sentences and paragraphs. Avoid writing large blocks of text if you want your message to be clear and easy to understand.
The reason for your email
Let's look at each of these in depth.
When you email someone for the first time, a compliment is a great start. A well-written compliment can also serve as an introduction.
"I found your blog on really useful. "
The reason for your email. In this section, you say, "I'm going to send an email to ask about ..." or "I was wondering if you could help with ..." You'll sometimes need two sentences to explain your reasons for writing.
"Could you write that in the next two weeks? "
However, when you have to be away for urgent reasons and you are unable to reach your boss, it is essential to write an e-mail containing the specific reasons for the absence as soon as possible. Similarly, when you know in advance that you need to address important personal or family issues, it is wise to write an email with your apology for the inconvenience and some clarification if possible.
When writing an excuse email to stay away, make sure you show that you care about the productivity of the company. It is not right to just say that you will be away, suggest doing something that will lessen the effects of your absence.
Please accept this email as an official notice that I was unable to attend 19 November 2018 due to a cold. Liam and Arthur took my place in my absence.
I have attached my medical certificate to this email.
Thank you for your understanding.
Please accept this e-mail as official notification that I will be away from work on 17 December 2018. I will appear as a professional witness in court that day.
Google takes into account several symbols or operators that can refine its search. These operators operate on the classic engine, Google Images and other variations of the search engine.
If you want to find web pages about end-of-year seminars for example that do not speak at the same time colloquia, just type "seminars end of the year - symposium". It is often annoying to look for information and get thousands of irrelevant results because of a namesake.
Also, if in doubt about the search, add an asterisk (*) to perform a special search and fill in the blanks of your query. This technique is practical and effective when one hesitates on the exact terms of the query and it works in most cases.
The "AND" command inserted between two terms will display all sites containing only one of them. As a Google search pro, you need to know that these commands can be combined for more precision and relevance in the search, some not excluding the others.
The search engine will display the sites containing the image in question and will also indicate similar images found. This functionality is useful to know the size, the sources of an image, to date with more or less precision the setting on line of this one.
To accelerate the search on the search engine, activate the instant search, adjust the number of results per page (ranging from 10 results per page to 50 or 100 results per page), open the results in a new window, block some sites, change the default language, or include multiple languages. By customizing the search parameters, you can also modify the geolocation by choosing a city or a country, an address, a postal code.
Google offers several tools that make it easy to search like:
Cache is an operator that allows you to view a page as it is saved in the Google cache. ( cache: nameofus );
Info is a tool for obtaining information about a site, accessing the cache of this site, similar pages and other advanced searches;
map displays the map of a locality;
Inblogtitle is also reserved for searching within blogs, but it limits the search to blog titles. Inposttitle limits the search to the titles of blog posts.
There is a lot of information on the web and it is not always easy to know how to get it. Yet a Google search pro directly type the query corresponding to its search and access sites public data such as GDP, mortality rate, life expectancy, military spending.
For those who want to convert a unit of value such as speed, distance between two points, currency, Google supports many systems and currencies. To convert a distance for example, simply type the value of this distance (20 kilometers for example) and convert it to another unit of value (in miles).
